From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:53:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] input: share creation while retaining device order

Use one window-input implementation for GPU and firmware displays.
Carry the desktop identities and screen-bound VNC device set from
Droid-VM 6455258e8d7eeb9050db3bc76dc14ed644b688a8. Preserve each
profile's existing pointer, touchscreen and keyboard ordering.

Include virtio-wl and GuestAccept for the existing shared desktop
profiles while retaining Linux's current device selection. The
firmware framebuffer beside a macOS GPU does not add another set
of input devices.

BUG=None
TEST=ARM64 release build; Linux and complete macOS argument matrices
TEST=Linux, shared desktop and VNC input identities/device-set test

Purpose: Share creation while retaining device order.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
